                <pb facs="0537" n="449" sameAs="frus:frus1933v04/pg449"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">721.23/994: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Venezuela</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Summerlin</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary
                        of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Caracas</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1933-02-03T17:00:00-04:30">February 3, 1933—5
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 7:12 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>2. Department’s circular telegram February 1, 7 p.m. The Foreign Office states
                    that it is now sending a telegram to Peru supporting the position taken by the
                    Department.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Summerlin</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
